{"skill":{"slug":"browserbase","displayName":"Browserbase Persist with captcha"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770748803191,"changelog":"Browserbase Sessions Skill 2.0.0\n\n- New skill to create and manage persistent Browserbase cloud browser sessions with authentication, captcha solving, and session recording.\n- Supports context-based authentication persistence, allowing users to stay logged in across sessions.\n- Enables browser automation: navigation, screenshots, JavaScript execution, and cookie management.\n- Provides workflow for setup, environment configuration, and running session management commands.\n- Includes session recording and playback, keep-alive features, and session logs for debugging and reproducibility.\n- Intended for automating logins, scraping authenticated pages, research documentation, and robust cloud browser management.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"references/api-quick-ref.md","size":2242,"sha256":"7e608d3f0f971fe9f17018579db3969b3b3c3114075f9467dd12331f7a8ae757","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":4024,"sha256":"76e906811a799ba77f2e0339d157cd2d2391f5e767e2fc8f080bc0b45e522242","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/browserbase_manager.py","size":33385,"sha256":"bda2517977121d0f110a4910e40dafde9155b9cf8b3fe69344a3c507f6966ccf","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","size":38,"sha256":"1c4b1667dbc3d0f74d897cca78aa6e6672e681360de39972f7506b572f05558e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10047,"sha256":"baf43321755684942ac217f3d460571281c02a2942d591bc8661d7bbe05d0294","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":3069,"sha256":"cb112664014fd8caa49098355ff5aaa7421cf4d3fb183b17a07698663e65d002","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789059265046,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9ad4c5b4e048f969048098f7743cb0abc74036560202b593dc5501415e663928","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9ad4c5b4e048f969048098f7743cb0abc74036560202b593dc5501415e663928","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: browserbase\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is designed for legitimate browser automation via the Browserbase service. It handles sensitive data like API keys, browser cookies, and can perform file operations (screenshots, recordings) to user-specified paths. The primary reason for 'suspicious' classification is the `execute-js` command in `scripts/browserbase_manager.py`, which allows the OpenClaw agent to execute arbitrary JavaScript code within the remote cloud browser session. While this is a core feature for browser automation, it presents a significant Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability if the agent's input is compromised via prompt injection, potentially leading to unauthorized actions or data exfiltration within the remote browser context. There is no evidence of intentional malicious behavior by the skill itself, such as exfiltrating data to unauthorized endpoints or installing backdoors on the local system.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162937600},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":20,"checkedAt":1789059265046},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill fits its Browserbase automation purpose, but it exposes active session secrets and cookies in normal output and records authenticated sessions by default.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to Browserbase and Browserbase credentials are expected for this skill, but default remote recording and logging of browser sessions are broader than needed for many workflows and may capture sensitive authenticated browsing.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is a normal Python dependency flow using pip or uv plus Playwright Chromium, but requirements use lower-bound-only versions, so future installs are not reproducible.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documentation discloses persistence, CAPTCHA solving, recording, JavaScript execution, and cookie access, but it does not adequately scope them by domain or warn that these actions can expose authenticated accounts. Arbitrary JavaScript and cookie export are powerful authenticated-session operations.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Authentication persistence is central and disclosed, with contexts stored by Browserbase and local friendly-name mappings stored under ~/.browserbase. The skill does not install system persistence, but long-lived contexts and keep-alive sessions preserve access to logged-in sites and need stronger user controls and warnings.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: create and manage Browserbase cloud browsers with auth persistence, screenshots, recordings, logs, JavaScript execution, and cookie access. The concern is that the implementation returns full cookies, connection URLs, debug URLs, and signing keys through ordinary JSON output without redaction or an explicit high-risk gate.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the agent control over Browserbase sessions that may stay logged in to websites. Avoid using it with sensitive accounts unless you disable recording, use separate contexts per site, delete contexts when finished, and avoid running get-cookies or live-url unless you intend to handle their output like credentials.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in part. Cookie access, recordings, logs, and debug/session URLs relate to browser management, but exposing full cookie values and access-bearing session URLs in default output is not proportionate.\n[RA2] expected: Downgraded from rogue-agent framing. Persistent Browserbase contexts and keep-alive sessions are explicitly part of the skill, but they remain sensitive because they preserve authenticated web access.\n[LP3] unexpected: Accepted as a review concern. The skill documents broad browser/session powers but lacks clear permission boundaries, domain scoping, or high-risk confirmations for cookies, debug URLs, and JavaScript execution.\n[MP3] expected: Overridden. The referenced context deletion is deletion of a Browserbase authentication context, not agent memory poisoning or safety-rule manipulation.\n[TM1] expected: Overridden. The DELETE context endpoint is a documented lifecycle command for this skill; the concern is permanence and user confirmation, not tool-parameter abuse.\n[E1] expected: Downgraded. Calls to api.browserbase.com are expected for a Browserbase integration and are not evidence of unrelated exfiltration.\n[SC1] unexpected: Accepted as a supply-chain note. The dependencies are legitimate-looking but unpinned, which weakens reproducibility for a skill handling browser sessions and credentials.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted. The script prints session-control URLs, signing keys, debug WebSocket URLs, and complete cookies to stdout, creating a realistic leakage path through logs or agent transcripts.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted as a lower-severity install risk. The package uses broad dependency constraints and no lockfile or hashes.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789059265046}}}}}